From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] CrySystem: build xml.cpp against expat older than 2.9

o3de/o3de#20170 (development, 2026-11-02) moved expat 2.9.0 in-tree and
switched the three line-number calls in xml.cpp to
XML_GetCurrentLineNumber64(), which first appeared in expat 2.9.0. With
system_expat on CentOS Stream 10 (expat 2.7.3) the call is undeclared and
the build fails. Map it to XML_GetCurrentLineNumber() when the expat
headers are older than 2.9; 2.9 and newer, including the in-tree copy,
are unchanged. Development counterpart of Patch0023.

--- a/Code/Legacy/CrySystem/XML/xml.cpp
+++ b/Code/Legacy/CrySystem/XML/xml.cpp
@@ -12,6 +12,11 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
 #include <expat.h>
+// XML_GetCurrentLineNumber64() first appeared in expat 2.9.0. Map it to the
+// older call when building against an earlier system expat (EL10 ships 2.7.3).
+#if XML_MAJOR_VERSION < 2 || (XML_MAJOR_VERSION == 2 && XML_MINOR_VERSION < 9)
+#define XML_GetCurrentLineNumber64(parser) XML_GetCurrentLineNumber(parser)
+#endif
 #include "xml.h"
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <stdio.h>
